--TEST--
`Core\Html::later` splices the text of a `Core\Html\Markup` its callable returned, and nothing from an object of any other class, whatever that object's first property contains — `rule:core-api/core-classes-are-sealed`
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class Fake {
    public string $text = "<script>x</script>";
}

var $markup = Core\Html::later(fn(): mixed => Core\Html::escape("<b>"));
echo $markup, "\n";

var $fake = Core\Html::later(fn(): mixed => new Fake());
echo "[", $fake, "]\n";
--EXPECT--
&lt;b&gt;
[]
